3, and incorporated in Maryland.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Bernard Francis Saul II | Chairman & CEO | Age 92 | Compensation: $159,000 (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 156 people. Revenue per employee of $1.9M ranks in the below the sector median among Real Estate peers. Stock-based compensation of $13K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 0\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (7/10).","financial_summary":["Saul Centers, Inc. is a small-cap real estate business with a $991M market cap on $290M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +6% over the past three years and +3% annually across the full decade, a respectable pace for a business of this size.","Returns on capital run at 8% against a 10% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests. Gross margins of 75% confirm genuine pricing power.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 1.8\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and thin 2.8\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Management returns a meaningful 5.4% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insiders hold 47% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is, and within its sector the business captures 3.4\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 207% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":2.0706100652939834},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.6) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Payout ratio looks stretched \u2014 the dividend\u2019s own margin of safety is thin","sev":"red","cat":"dividend"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Interest-rate sensitivity and tenant-credit risk \u2014 cap rates and refinancing costs move faster than the 10-year leases can absorb.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Remote work structural vacancy \u2014 the post-pandemic shift to hybrid work has permanently impaired demand for urban office space across most markets.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Climate and insurance cost escalation \u2014 rising premiums and coverage withdrawals in flood/fire zones are repricing assets that the market once treated as perpetuities.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Operating margins 45% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power","Trading near the bottom of its 52-week range \u2014 the market is offering a discount","32 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Gross margin tops the Real Estate peer set \u2014 genuine pricing power is present here","Real Estate sector outperforming the broader market over the past quarter"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Saul Centers (NYSE:BFS) Sets New 52-Week Low \u2013 Here\u2019s Why","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/06/saul-centers-nysebfs-sets-new-52-week-low-heres-why.html","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793980855.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.226,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Is Saul Centers (BFS) Undervalued Based On Its Cash Flow?","source":"simplywall.st","link